      "side": 0,
      "message": "I am not sure... I looked up https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/uses-sdk-element, and it says\n```\nandroid:targetSdkVersion\nAn integer designating the API Level that the application targets. If not set, the default value equals that given to minSdkVersion.\n```\n\nIf `targetSdkVersion` is missing in the manifest file, it defaults to `minSdkVersion`. So I suppose this is WAI, but I am not sure why this is the intended behavior. Maybe to ensure backwards compatibility when the app is installed on an older device?\n\n+ccross, do you know why we do not use the api level of `sdk_version` here?",
